      "side": 1,
      "message": "Rabbit Hole:\n\nThere is a python package called platformdirs https://platformdirs.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api.html#windows which has variables for various types of dirs on different platforms. Their docs led me to https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/shell/knownfolderid which lists a bunch of known folders on Windows. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.environment.specialfolder?view\u003dnet-9.0\u0026redirectedfrom\u003dMSDN has a list of them that show up in the environment. That can be used from PowerShell like:\n\n  [Environment]::GetFolderPath(\"ApplicationData\")\n\nPerhaps ApplicationData/Zuul would be more like the global /tmp/ than All Users/Zuul? I see cache files and other program specific but ephemeral files there.",
      "revId": "3c9378b897e6460380ab6da3493becbd41d75435",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6dd6b080_4e579ae1",
        "filename": "zuul/ansible/base/library/win_zuul_console.ps1",
