      "writtenOn": "2025-03-31T17:17:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ApplicationData resolves to: C:\\Users\\\u003cusername\u003e\\AppData\\Roaming which won\u0027t work because it\u0027s specific to the user.\n\nBut platformdirs.Windows.site_data_dir is C:\\ProgramData\\Zuul\\Zuul -- which is the same directory (via links) as C:\\Users\\All Users\\Zuul\\Zuul.  It\u0027s advocating an \"author/program\" hierarchy, so the first Zuul is the author, and the second is the program.  I\u0027m not sure that the extra level is necessary for us.\n\nIn the MSDN docs, Environment.SpecialFolder.CommonApplicationData resolves to C:\\ProgramData -- so I think that\u0027s equivalent.\n\nThat all suggests to me that we did find the right place, but perhaps changing the path to C:\\ProgramData\\Zuul (or C:\\ProgramData\\Zuul\\Zuul ?) would be a more standard name.",
      "parentUuid": "fdfc9b24_36eb07bc",
      "revId": "3c9378b897e6460380ab6da3493becbd41d75435",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
